[
    {
        "content": "<p>I just got myself confused about running a command with a modified scope.  Here are the two relevant definitions (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Command.modifyScope#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Command.modifyScope</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Command.withScope#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Command.withScope</a>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modifyScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scope</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">modify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">scopes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">scopes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unreachable!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">withScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Scope</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElabM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">scopes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">modify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scopes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">modify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">scopes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Judging from the name, I would guess that, to first approximation, <code>withScope</code> would modify the scope as <code>modifyScope</code> would and then would act with whatever you pass it.</p>\n<p>This does not seem to be the case, though, unless I am even more confused!</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Init</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- warns, as expected</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"modify_scope \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getOptions</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">modifyScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`linter.unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">elabCommand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"with_scope \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getOptions</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`linter.unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">elabCommand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">modify_scope</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- silent, as expected</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">with_scope</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- shouldn't this be silenced?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 590482553,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776953255
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A guess without running anything: I think linters are run by the top-level command elaborator, so setting <code>linter.unusedTactic</code> locally won't have any effect. I'd guess <code>modify_scope</code> works since the scope remains modified, so the top-level command elaborator sees that as the current options state.</p>",
        "id": 590490113,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776954997
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Presumably the linter should be re-checking the options from the infotree at the point of the tactic? That is, this should work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Init</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- shouldn't this be silenced?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 590490528,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776955080
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another datapoint:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"modify_scope \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getOptions</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">modifyScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`linter.unusedSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">elabCommand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"with_scope \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getOptions</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withScope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">opts</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`linter.unusedSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">elabCommand</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">modify_scope</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- silent</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedSimpArgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">with_scope</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- silent</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 590490624,
        "sender_full_name": "fiforeach",
        "timestamp": 1776955101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was about to comment that the <code>unusedVariables</code> option <em>can</em> be silenced in those ways.</p>",
        "id": 590490800,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955139
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That linter option is checked by <code>simp</code> itself during its operation, so that makes senes <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1006462\">@fiforeach</span>.</p>",
        "id": 590490809,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776955141
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Both <code>simp</code> and <code>unusedVariables</code> are infotree based, right?</p>",
        "id": 590491023,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955184
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, but you have to re-check if the linter is enabled as you recurse (edit: no, the simp linter isn't a linter at all IIUC, the tactic just emits lint warnings at runtime)</p>",
        "id": 590491135,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776955207
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not enough to check just once before you start</p>",
        "id": 590491181,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776955215
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Eric, in your example I can understand that the option that you are setting expires before you are able to know the answer to the question, so I would be happy to give up on it.</p>",
        "id": 590491535,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955284
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could it be an issue with linters in core vs linters not in core?</p>",
        "id": 590492176,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955418
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think it's easy, when you analyze the goals before and after the tactic you also know if the option is set</p>",
        "id": 590492186,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776955420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"321459\">@Damiano Testa</span> Interesting, while <code>simp</code> actually checks the linter option while it evaluates the tactic (in <code>Lean.Elab.Tactic.evalSimp</code>), it pushes infotree nodes to record the results, and then <code>Lean.Linter.unusedSimpArgs</code> appears to check the global state of the linter option to decide whether to report it.</p>",
        "id": 590492262,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776955439
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Kyle, that is what I thought as well, though I am glad for the confirmation!</p>",
        "id": 590492418,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that something similar happens for <code>unusedVariables</code>.</p>",
        "id": 590492554,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955509
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the logic is usually that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">badthing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">badthing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">bad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- silent as expected</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>works, but</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">badthing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">badthing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">bad</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- silent, but should be noisy</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is unsupported for performance</p>",
        "id": 590492611,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776955519
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It also pushes to the a custominfo in the infotrees, I think.</p>",
        "id": 590492617,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955521
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Eric, I did not know that this was a performance optimisation!</p>",
        "id": 590493042,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955616
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Regarding the unused <code>simp</code>, I think that the logic there is that a simp argument may be used by a branch of a proof, but not another (e.g. in the presence of <code>tac &lt;;&gt; simp [x]</code>), so the linter waits until the end and reads off the final infotree node to figure out whether an argument was used or not.  The <code>unusedVariables</code> probably has a similar behaviour, since you have to wait until the very end to know which variables actually enter the final term.</p>",
        "id": 590493582,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955746
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Anyway, I am happy to use <code>modifyScope</code> instead of <code>withScope</code>, but it took me a while to figure out that this was doable, since I kept using <code>withScope</code> and getting confused!</p>",
        "id": 590493932,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776955827
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Damiano, do you specifically care about this linter only?</p>",
        "id": 590499439,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776957051
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I cared about the unusedTactic and unreachableTactic linters particularly, yes.</p>",
        "id": 590499592,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1776957086
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"306601\">@Kyle Miller</span> , should</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">builtin_tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Parser</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set_option</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabSetOption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elabSetOption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withOptions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`diagnostics</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">reportDiag</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>be adding a context  to the infotree with modified options?</p>",
        "id": 590531690,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776966231
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The fix I attempted in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38425\">#38425</a> suggests that the context isn't actually changing</p>",
        "id": 590532146,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776966351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, it seems plausible that the updated options should be captured in the tree. Possibly <code>TacticInfo</code> itself could capture the current options, though a full context node would be sufficient.</p>",
        "id": 590536920,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1776967662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed changing to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elabSetOption</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">withOptions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">options</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">withSaveInfoContext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">finally</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`diagnostics</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">reportDiag</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>fixes it</p>",
        "id": 590540336,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776968762
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess for efficiency it would make sense to have a <code>PartialContextInfo.optionsCtx</code> constructor?</p>",
        "id": 590540417,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776968793
    }
]